{#-
  BLOCK: grid — the wrappers that arrange gallery cards on the page.

  Not one of §06's eight named blocks: it is what remained in Python once the
  cards themselves became blocks, and leaving it there would have meant the last
  five functions in this module still held HTML. A `<table>` deciding that two
  cards sit side by side is markup.

  `.mobile-stack` on the cells is B4 and is load-bearing. That rule stacks the
  columns at 320px and was defined in the document's <style> block while being
  attached to zero elements, so a two-across grid stayed two-across on a phone.

  Cards arrive rendered. This block places them and knows nothing about what a
  card contains, which is why the same wrapper serves the 2-across and 3-across
  layouts with only `per_row` differing.
-#}
{% if shape == 'rows' -%}
              <div style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
                {{ cards | join('') }}
              </div>
{%- else -%}
              <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%" style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
                {% for row in rows %}
                <tr>
                  {%- for cell in row %}
                  <td width="{{ cell_width }}" class="mobile-stack" style="{{ cell.pad }} vertical-align: top;">{{ cell.html }}</td>
                  {%- endfor %}
                </tr>
                {%- endfor %}
              </table>
{%- endif %}
